Package: flatstitch
Version: 1.1.0-1
Section: graphics
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.9), python3-venv, python3-pip, python3-tk
Recommends: python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0
Suggests: python3-pyqt5
Installed-Size: 524
Maintainer: kar_ton <p.nikita.u@gmail.com>
Description: Stitch flat scanned images into one seamless TIFF
 flatstitch registers and blends overlapping flatbed-scanner tiles
 (technical drawings, maps, documents) into a single seamless TIFF.
 Unlike general panorama tools (Hugin, Microsoft ICE), it fits a rigid
 rotation+translation model instead of a full homography, matching the
 physical reality of a flat scan and avoiding needless perspective
 distortion of straight lines and text.
 .
 Includes a command-line tool (flatstitch) and a graphical interface
 (flatstitch-gui, also in the application menu) that adapts to your
 desktop: native GTK3 on GNOME, Cinnamon, XFCE, MATE and LXDE, native Qt5
 on KDE Plasma and LXQt (needs python3-pyqt5), and a Tk interface
 everywhere else. Available in 10 languages (auto-detected, or chosen
 explicitly): English, Ukrainian, Spanish, French, German, Portuguese
 (Brazil), Italian, Polish, Simplified Chinese and Japanese.
 .
 This package downloads its Python dependencies (OpenCV, NumPy, SciPy,
 tifffile and others) into a private virtual environment the first time
 it is configured, so an internet connection is required during
 installation and initial setup may take a few minutes.
